; A `;@axiom:deprecated(...)` value containing parentheses of its own.
;
; Four readers slice an AXTAG value: `checkOneAxtag`, `symbols.ax`'s
; `saAxMeta`, `format.ax`'s `fpAxtag`, and `axtagTextValue` - which
; `axtagValueOf`, and so AX3048, are built on. Three used the LAST `)`;
; the fourth stopped at the FIRST, so a replacement written as a call
; reached the warning with a paren missing. Measured on the compiler
; before the change: the label read `;@axiom:deprecated(use (newLen v)`
; and the help "the declaration says: use (newLen v". The whole value
; is what the author wrote, and that is what both fields quote now.
;@axiom:deprecated(use (newLen v) instead)
(pub :: oldLen (-> Int Int))

(pub fn (oldLen v) 0)

(:: newLen (-> Int Int))

(fn (newLen v) 1)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (oldLen 7) (newLen 7)))
